{"author":{"id":"7be502fc1252faa17034e20337c97f83224cb75681f6f2358da33e4e8d7e55b6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794790604,"nonce":"zrsXbH9t1I7R540V8GntQm2Cj74=","title":"Feature request: apply header policies (CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy) to static-files routes","message":"Hello Zentinel team,\n\nthank you for Zentinel. This is a low-priority feature request: response header rules currently do not apply to answers from `static-files` routes.\n\nObserved (tag 26.11_2, commit ea8ccf0), tested with Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options and Referrer-Policy on a static route:\n\n- route `policies { response-headers { set ... } }`: none of the headers appear in the response\n- a `headers` filter on the route, with phase response and with phase both: none appear\n- a filter attached to a namespace listener serving the same static route: none appear\n- the same `policies response-headers` on a route with an upstream (a small file server on localhost): all three headers appear\n\nCause as far as we can tell: route policies for response headers are applied in response_filter (crates/proxy/src/proxy/http_trait.rs:2495-2497). A static route is answered directly in handle_static_route, which writes the response itself and returns Ok(true) to skip the upstream path (crates/proxy/src/proxy/handlers.rs:31-99), so the header rules do not seem to be reached.\n\nRequest: please apply the configured header rules (policies response-headers and headers filters) to responses of static-files routes as well, or offer an equivalent setting. This would allow a Content-Security-Policy and nosniff to be set for purely static sites without an extra upstream.\n\nHappy to test a fix. Thank you.","files":null}]}